Port patch 0011 - report every relocated fragment to the host
Why: the port runs the C code of the code overlays natively and maps a call into a loaded overlay to the native function
(src/platform/host_fragment.c). It found the overlay through gFragments, but that table keeps ONE entry per id: the battle scene loads
an arena file and later another file from the same archive (same id), which replaces the entry although the first file's code stays in
the pool and is called afterwards (found by running the game: "call into the memory pool outside any loaded fragment"). The loader
now also reports each relocated fragment (id, address, size) to the host, which keeps its own list of the extents.

--- a/src/memmap.c
+++ b/src/memmap.c
@@ -8,6 sha256=3bca9ceed442a0f0ca76fb162016deda25d756146bb1a7f5427d6e50b892a075 @@
=3
+
+/* PORT: tells the host where a fragment's code now lives (src/platform/host_fragment.c). gFragments is not enough for that: a later load
+ * with the same id replaces the entry, although the earlier fragment's code stays in the pool and is still called (the arena files of
+ * the battle scene are such fragments). */
+void HostNoteFragmentLoaded(u32 id, void* fragment, u32 size);
=3
@@ -105,6 sha256=a440f6dd67cd18164548a7e20e4c68f21bf5749c72b622319ee0d62429708f7f @@
=3
+    HostNoteFragmentLoaded(id, fragment, fragment->sizeInRam);
=3
